hadiths[199]{hadithnumber,text}:
"109","""I was a hidden treasure; I desired to be known, so I created the creation."
"110","""Neither My earth contained Me nor My heaven, but the heart of My believing servant contained Me. (That is, I dwell in the heart of My believing servant)."
"111","""Indeed, with the Most Merciful there is a tablet, in which there are three hundred and fifteen (315) laws. The Most Merciful, Mighty and Majestic, says: By My honor and majesty! Whoever of My servants comes to Me in such a state that he does not associate anyone with Me, and possesses any one of these laws, will enter Paradise."
"112","""I have created good and evil. So glad tidings are for the one in whose hand I have destined good, and destruction is for the one in whose hand I have destined evil."
"113","""Whoever affirmed My Oneness has entered My fortress, and whoever has entered My fortress is safe from My punishment."
"114","""I am Allah, I have created the servants according to My knowledge. So, whomever I intend good for, I grant him a good creation (form and appearance), and whomever I intend evil for, I grant him an evil creation."
"115","""There are some of My servants whose faith cannot remain correct without wealth, and if I make them poor, they would fall into disbelief. And there are some of My servants whose faith cannot remain correct without poverty, and if I make them wealthy, they would fall into disbelief."
"116","""O son of Adam! Perform two rak'ahs at the beginning of the day and I guarantee you (deliverance from every difficulty) in the last part of the day."
"117","""Indeed, when a servant performs prayer well in both public and private circumstances, Allah Almighty says: This is My true servant."
"118","""Whoever among the elders safeguards three things is my true friend, and whoever neglects them is my true enemy (and they are): prayer, fasting, and the ritual bath of impurity (ghusl janabat)."
"119","""Indeed, I intend to send punishment upon the people of the earth, but when I look at those among them who are building My house purely out of love for Me, and those who seek forgiveness at the time of dawn, I turn (the punishment) away from them."
"120","“When Allah Almighty created the earth, the earth began to move. Then Allah created the mountains and placed them upon the earth, and thus the earth became stable. The angels were amazed at the strength of the mountains and asked, ‘O Lord, is there any of Your creation stronger than the mountains?’ Allah said, ‘Yes! Iron is.’ They asked, ‘O Lord, is there any of Your creation stronger than iron?’ Allah said, ‘Yes! Fire is.’ Then they asked, ‘O Lord, is there anything in Your creation stronger than fire?’ Allah said, ‘Yes! Water is.’ Then they asked, ‘O Lord, is there anything in Your creation stronger than water?’ Allah said, ‘Yes! Wind is.’ They then asked, ‘O Lord, is there anything in Your creation stronger than wind?’ Allah said, ‘Yes! The son of Adam who gives charity with his right hand and conceals it from his left hand.’”"
"121","""If a servant falls asleep in prostration, Allah boasts about him before the angels, saying: 'Look at My servant; his soul is with Me and his body (still) remains in My obedience.'"
"122","""I have created one hundred thousand communities, and no community knows that I have created any community besides itself."
"123","The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) recited this verse: ""Is the reward for good anything but good?"" and said, ""Do you know what your Lord has said?"" The companions replied, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says that for the one upon whom I have bestowed the blessing of monotheism, the only reward is Paradise."
"124","""Bring those who recite the Kalimah La ilaha illallah close to the shade of My Throne, for I love them."
"125","""It is written on the Throne that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, Muhammad (peace be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah. Whoever says this statement, I will not punish him."
"126","""Sincerity is a secret; I entrust it to the heart of whomsoever I love among My servants."
"127","""I have sworn that whoever recites (Surah Fatiha, Ayat al-Kursi, the two verses of Aal-e-Imran 'Shahida Allah... to the end' and «قل اللهم مالك الملك» ... to the end) after every prayer, I will make Paradise his abode."
"128","""I am honorable; whoever desires honor in this world and the Hereafter should obey (me), the honorable one."
"129","""Do not consider insignificant the person to whom I have granted knowledge, because I have not considered him insignificant (that is why I have granted him knowledge)."
"130","""The generous person is from me and I am from him (that is, our mutual relationship is strong), and indeed I make the punishment of the grave easy for the generous person."
"131","""On the Day of Resurrection, Allah Almighty will say: 'Where are My neighbors?' Upon hearing this, the angels will submit, 'O Lord! Who can be Your neighbor?' Then Allah Almighty will say: 'Where are the reciters of the Qur'an and those who built mosques?' (That is, these people are My neighbors)."
"132","""Whoever, due to being engaged in the recitation of the Qur'an, was unable to ask Me (for anything) through supplication, I will grant him a reward superior to those who are grateful."
"133","""Beware of arrogance, for indeed a servant continues to be arrogant until Allah, the Exalted, says: 'Record this servant of Mine among the rebellious ones.'"
"134","""Allah Almighty commanded the world: Serve the one who serves Me, and tire out the one who serves you."
"135","""(O Prophet!) If you had not been, Allah Almighty would not have created the Throne, the Chair, the earth, the heavens, the sun, the moon, or anything else besides them."
"136","""Whoever speaks at the time of the adhan, there is a fear that his faith may be lost."
"137","""Three things are the essence of faith: to withhold your hand from one who says «لا اله الا الله» , not to declare him a disbeliever because of any sin, and not to expel him from Islam because of any deed. Jihad has been ongoing since my prophethood and will continue until the last group of my Ummah fights against the Dajjal; neither the oppression of any oppressor nor the justice of any just person can invalidate it. Belief in destiny."
"138","""When a believer is praised to his face, his faith increases."
"139","""The most honorable faith is that people remain safe from you."
"140","""The best faith is that you have the conviction that wherever you are, Allah Almighty is with you."
"141","""Iman is a garment; Allah bestows this garment upon whomsoever He wills. So when a servant commits adultery, Allah removes the garment of iman from him, and if he repents, He returns it to him."
"142","""Iman is bare, its clothing is piety, its adornment is modesty, and its fruit is knowledge."
"143","""Indeed, modesty is from faith and foul language is from hypocrisy."
"144","""The whiteness of the head due to old age is the garment of faith."
"145","""Iman has sixty-four (64) doors."
"146","""Belief in destiny removes (all) worries and sorrows."
"147","""Iman is the name of heartfelt intention and verbal affirmation, and Hijrah is that which is done with wealth and life."
"148","""Iman protects from forbidden matters and places of greed."
"149","""Faith is two halves: one half is in patience and the other half is in gratitude."
"150","""Faith and deeds are two brothers. Allah Almighty does not accept either of them without its companion."
"151","""It is sufficient for a person’s faith that he says: I am pleased with Allah as my Lord, with Muhammad (peace be upon him) as His Messenger, and with Islam as my religion."
"152","""Use the toothstick (miswak), for it is cleanliness, and cleanliness leads to faith, and faith leads its possessor to Paradise."
"153","""Whoever possesses three things, his reward becomes obligatory and his faith is complete: such character through which he lives among people; such piety that prevents him from what Allah has forbidden; and such forbearance and patience that protects him from the ignorance of the ignorant."
"154","""Five things are part of faith; if a person does not possess any one of them, his faith is not correct: accepting Allah's command, being content with Allah's decision, entrusting matters to Allah, relying on Allah, and being patient at the onset of calamity."
"155","""Love for Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, is a part of faith, while hatred towards them is disbelief; love for the Ansar is a part of faith, while hatred towards them is disbelief; love for the Arabs is a part of faith, while hatred towards them is disbelief."
"156","""Envy corrupts faith just as colocynth (a bitter herb) spoils honey."
"157","""Miswak is half of faith and ablution is half of faith."
"158","""Patience holds the same position in faith as the head does in the body."
"159","""Patience is half of faith, while certainty is complete faith."
"160","""The believers are the gentlest of all people in killing (and slaughtering)."
"161","""Prayer is the pillar of faith, and striving (jihad) is the hump of action, and charity (zakat) is between the two."
"162","""Adopt woolen clothing, you will find the sweetness of faith in your hearts."
"163","""Knowledge is the life of Islam and the pillar of faith."
"164","""Just as nothing is of benefit in the presence of shirk, likewise nothing is harmful in the presence of faith."
"165","""Everything has a foundation, and the foundation of faith is piety (taqwa)."
"166","""Everything has an essence, and the essence of faith is prayer, and the essence of prayer is the opening Takbeer (Takbeer-e-Tahreema)."
"167","""A believer's faith is not complete until he considers trial as a blessing and prosperity as a calamity."
"168","""The example of faith is like that of a shirt; you wear it and you also take it off."
"169","""Whoever drinks alcohol, Allah removes faith from him in the same way that a person takes off his shirt from over his head."
"170","""Whoever goes for the Fajr prayer in the morning is holding the banner of faith, and whoever goes to the market in the morning is holding the banner of Iblis."
"171","""Medina is the dome of Islam and the abode of faith."
"172","""A servant cannot attain the reality of faith until he restrains his tongue."
"173","Someone asked the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), ""What is the best form of faith?"" He (peace be upon him) replied: ""Migration."
"174","""He who does not remember Allah abundantly is outside of faith."
"175","""He who has no modesty has no faith."
"176","“Backbiting and tale-bearing shake off faith just as a shepherd shakes leaves off a tree for his animals.”"
"177","""Love for one's homeland is a part of faith."
"178","""Love for the cat is a part of faith."
"179","""Faith is embedded in the heart like strong mountains; any increase or decrease in it is disbelief."
"180","""The delegation of Thaqif came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and asked: 'Does faith increase and decrease?' He (peace be upon him) replied: 'No, faith is complete in the heart; increase in it is disbelief and decrease in it is polytheism.'"
"181","""Neither does faith increase nor does it decrease."
"182","""A person cannot have complete faith until he gives up lying even in jest, and gives up quarrelling even if he is in the right."
"183","""Whoever doubted his faith, his deeds were ruined and he will be among the losers in the Hereafter."
"184","""Paradise becomes obligatory for the one at whose hand a person accepts Islam."
"185","""Whoever said: If Allah wills, I am a believer, then he has no share in Islam."
"186","""A perfect believer is one who says 'InshaAllah' in everything he says."
"187","""He who is not a true believer is certainly a true disbeliever."
"188","""The most enviable among My friends in terms of rank and status, in my view, is that believer who is thin and attains a large portion of prayer."
"189","""If the fear and hope of a believer are weighed, both will be equal."
"190","""Whoever rebukes an innovator, Allah Almighty fills his heart with peace and faith."
"191","""Allah Almighty created the horse and made it run; it began to sweat, so Allah Almighty created His own self from that sweat."
"192","""There are seventy thousand veils between Allah and the creation."
"193","""Allah Almighty has created one thousand nations; out of them, six hundred are in the sea and four hundred on land."
"194","""The heart is the house of the Lord."
"195","""Think about everything, but do not think about the Essence of Allah."
"196","""All creation is the family of Allah, and the most beloved to Allah among them is the one who is most beneficial to His family."
"197","""If there were no women, Allah would have been worshipped as He truly deserves."
"198","""If there were no women, men would enter Paradise."
"199","""The parents of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) were brought to life until they believed in him (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"200","""First, Allah Almighty created the Pen, then He created Nun, and that is the inkpot. This is mentioned in the statement of Allah Almighty «ن ، والقلم وما يسطرون» ."
"201","""When Adam (peace be upon him) committed a sin, he said: O Lord! I ask You for forgiveness by the right of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). Allah Almighty said: O Adam! How did you know about Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) when I have not yet created him? Adam (peace be upon him) said: O Lord! When You created me with Your own hand and breathed into me of Your spirit, I raised my head and saw that it was written on the pillars of the Throne: 'There is no god but Allah, Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.' I knew that the one whose name You have joined with Yours is the most beloved of all creation to You. Allah Almighty said: O Adam! You have spoken the truth. Indeed, he is the most beloved to Me among creation, so call upon Me by his right. Surely, I have forgiven you, and if it were not for Muhammad, I would not have created you."
"202","“Dawud (peace be upon him) said: O Allah! I ask You by the means of my forefathers Ibrahim, Ishaq, and Yaqub.”"
"203","""When you ask Allah Almighty, then ask through the means of my rank and status."
"204","Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) submitted, ""O Messenger of Allah! May my parents be sacrificed for you, tell me about the first thing which Allah Almighty created before all things."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""O Jabir! Allah Almighty created the light of your Prophet from His own light before all things, and He gave this light such power that, by His might, it would move wherever Allah willed. At that time, there was neither the Preserved Tablet nor the Pen, nor Paradise nor Hell, nor any angel, nor earth and sky, nor sun and moon, nor jinn nor mankind."
"205","""I am (a light) from the Light of Allah, and the believers are from me. Goodness is from me, and in my Ummah until the Day of Judgment."
"206","""I was a Prophet even when Adam (peace be upon him) was between water and clay."
"207","""The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to see in the dark just as he saw in the light."
"208","""The family of Muhammad is entirely pious."
"209","""The shadow of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was not visible in the sunlight nor in the moonlight."
"210","""Indeed, Allah Almighty spoke to Musa (peace be upon him), and He granted me His vision, bestowed upon me the Maqam Mahmood, and granted me the Hawd al-Kawthar upon which the believers will come."
"211","""When I was taken on the journey to the heavens (that is, on the night of Mi'raj), I saw my Lord. There was a visible veil between me and Him. I saw everything of my Lord, even the crown."
"212","""I saw my Lord at Mina riding a camel, wearing a cloak."
"213","""Whoever visits my grave, intercession becomes obligatory for him."
"214","""Recite blessings upon me in abundance on the day of Friday. It is a day on which the angels are present, and whoever sends blessings upon me, his voice reaches me wherever he may be."" We asked, ""Even after your passing?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) replied, ""Even after my passing. Indeed, Allah the Exalted has forbidden the earth to consume the bodies of the Prophets."
"215","""I am the Seal of the Prophets; there is no prophet after me, except if Allah wills."
"216","Hazrat Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sent him to Yemen, he asked him, ""When cases are presented before you, how will you decide them?"" He replied, ""I will decide according to the Book of Allah."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""If the matter is not found in the Book of Allah?"" He replied, ""Then I will decide according to the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) again said, ""If the matter is not found in the Sunnah of the Messenger either?"" He replied, ""Then I will exercise my own judgment (ijtihad) and will not spare any effort."" Upon this, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) struck his chest with his hand and said, ""All praise is due to Allah Who has granted the messenger of the Messenger of Allah the ability to do that which pleases the Messenger of Allah."
"217","""Indeed, after me there will be some people who will narrate hadiths from me. You should examine their narrated hadiths against the Qur'an; accept those which are in accordance with the Qur'an, and do not accept those which are not in accordance with the Qur'an."
"218","""When you write a hadith, write it along with its chain of narration."
"219","""Allah Almighty denies the authenticity of every book except the Qur'an."
"220","""My word cannot abrogate the word of Allah, but the word of Allah can abrogate my word."
"221","""Whoever memorizes forty hadiths regarding the religious matters of my Ummah, Allah Almighty will raise him (on the Day of Resurrection) as a jurist."
"222","""When a hadith is narrated to you which you recognize, then accept it, and when a hadith is narrated to you which you find unfamiliar, then do not accept it."
"223","""When innovations become widespread and the last people of this Ummah begin to curse its first ones, then whoever possesses knowledge should spread and disseminate it."
"224","""Whoever conveys to my Ummah a hadith that establishes a Sunnah or eliminates a Bid'ah, then for him is Paradise."
"225","""Whoever goes to a heretic with the intention of honoring him has assisted in the destruction of Islam."
"226","""Whoever turns away from an innovator out of hatred for him, Allah Almighty fills his heart with peace and faith."
"227","""When an innovator dies, Islam attains victory."
"228","""Every innovation is misguidance except innovation in worship."
"229","""Innovators are the worst of the creatures."
"230","""There will be a man in my Ummah whose name will be Muhammad bin Idris (that is, Imam Shafi'i), he will be more harmful to my Ummah than Iblis. And there will be a man in my Ummah named Abu Hanifa, he will be the lamp of my Ummah."
"231","""My Ahl al-Bayt are like stars; whichever of them you follow, you will be guided."
"232","""Follow the scholars, for they are the lamps of the world and the lanterns of the Hereafter."
"233","""Salman is from among our Ahl al-Bayt."
"234","""Whoever speaks in our religion based on his own opinion, kill him."
"235","""Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) is the best of mankind; whoever denied it has committed disbelief."
"236","""If people were to know when Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) was given the title of Amir al-Mu'minin, they would not deny his virtue. Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) was given the title of Amir al-Mu'minin at a time when Adam (peace be upon him) was still between soul and body."
"237","""O Ali! You are my brother in this world and the Hereafter."
"238","""Ali is the leader of the righteous and the slayer of the wicked. Whoever helps him will be helped, and whoever tries to disgrace him will be disgraced."
"239","""O Ali! I am the Seal of the Prophets and you are the Seal of the Saints."
"240","""Love the Quraysh, surely whoever loves them, Allah Almighty will love him."
"241","""Love for the Quraysh is faith and hatred for them is disbelief, and love for the Arabs is faith and hatred for them is disbelief."
"242","""The Prophet (peace be upon him) named his daughter Fatimah (the one who prevents) because Allah, the Exalted, has prevented her and those who love her from the Fire."
"243","""(O Fatimah!) Allah Almighty will neither punish you nor your children."
"244","""On the Day of Resurrection, Islam will be raised in the form of a man."
"245","""The world is the cultivation field for the Hereafter."
"246","""The grave is either a garden from the gardens of Paradise or a pit from the pits of Hell."
"247","""When the deceased is placed in the grave, the grave calls out to him and says: O son of Adam! You are doomed, what deceived you concerning me? Did you not know that I am the house of darkness, trials, and loneliness?"
"248","""The grave calls out to you five times a day."
"249","""There will be neither any terror in the grave for the people of monotheism nor on the Day of Resurrection."
"250","""Whoever visits the grave of his parents or one of them every Friday will be forgiven."
"251","""Whoever visits the graves of his parents every Friday and recites Surah Yaseen by them, he will be granted forgiveness equal to the number of all verses and all letters."
"252","""Looking at a beautiful face sharpens the eyesight."
"253","""Looking at a beautiful face is an act of worship."
"254","""Seek goodness and virtue near beautiful faces."
"255","""If one seeks forgiveness, even major sins do not remain, and if one persists in sin, even minor sins become major."
"256","“Gabriel (peace be upon him) came to me and said: O Muhammad! Allah Almighty sends you greetings of peace and says: By My honor and majesty! O Muhammad! I will not punish in the fire of Hell any person whose name is upon your name.”"
"257","""Caliphate is in Medina while monarchy is in Syria."
"258","""A child born as a result of adultery will not enter Paradise."
"259","""Indeed, for the companion of the Qur'an, there is an accepted supplication at the completion of every recitation of the Qur'an."
"260","""Trial is attached to speech (i.e., silence is a means of safety for a person, and speaking is a cause of trial)."
"261","""The best deed is the one in which there is moderation."
"262","""If any one of you entertains good thoughts even about a stone, it will benefit him."
"263","""The intention of a believer is better than his action."
"264","""Whoever fell in love, remained chaste, concealed it, and died, then he died the death of a martyr."
"265","""Burying daughters is among the commendable deeds."
"266","""The one who has died, his Resurrection has begun."
"267","""Keep accounting of your own selves before you are called to account."
"268","""After the Prophets and martyrs, the first person to be clothed will be Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"269","""The scholars of my Ummah are like the prophets of the Children of Israel."
"270","""Whoever followed a scholar in imitation will meet Allah Almighty in a state of safety."
"271","""The calamity of knowledge is forgetting it."
"272","""Whoever sets out in search of knowledge remains in the path of Allah until he returns."
"273","""A single jurist is more severe upon Satan than a thousand worshippers."
"274","""The superiority of a scholar over a worshipper is like my superiority over one of my followers."
"275","""Whoever writes down from me any matter of knowledge or a hadith, reward will continue to be written for him as long as that knowledge or hadith remains."
"276","""The greatest generous person among the people after me is the one who acquired knowledge and then spread and disseminated his knowledge."
"277","""When the Day of Resurrection comes, golden pulpits will be placed. Then a caller from the Most Merciful will proclaim: Where are those who conveyed knowledge to the Ummah of Muhammad, and they did this solely for the pleasure of Allah? (It will be said to them:) Sit upon these pulpits and enter Paradise."
"278","""Indeed, a person's betrayal in knowledge is more severe than his betrayal in wealth."
"279","""Do not throw pearls, that is, knowledge, into the mouths of dogs."
"280","""Entrust knowledge to new people."
"281","""If a day comes upon me in which I do not increase in knowledge, then let there be no blessing in the rising of the sun on that day."
"282","""Four things are never satisfied with four things: the eye with seeing, the earth with rain, the female with the male, and the scholar with knowledge."
"283","""Flattery and sycophancy are not among the morals of a believer, except if he does so in the pursuit of knowledge."
"284","""When a teacher tells a child to say 'Bismillah' and the child says 'Bismillah', Allah Almighty writes freedom from Hell for the child, his parents, and the teacher (because of this)."
"285","""The worst among you are your teachers; they show the least mercy to the orphan."
"286","""Attending gatherings of knowledge is better than attending a thousand funerals."
"287","""The wages of teachers, muezzins, and imams are forbidden."
"288","""Do not sit with every scholar, only sit with that scholar who calls from five things to five things: from doubt to certainty, from enmity to goodwill, from arrogance to humility, from ostentation to sincerity, from desire for the world to indifference towards the world."
"289","""When a hadith is narrated to you from me and it is in accordance with the truth, then accept it, whether I have narrated it or not."
"290","""Whoever teaches a slave one verse becomes his master."
"291","""There are two types of knowledge: physical knowledge (such as medicine, etc.) and religious knowledge."
"292","""There are two types of knowledge: one is the knowledge that is in the heart, and that is beneficial knowledge; and the other is the knowledge of the tongue, and that is Allah's proof against the son of Adam."
"293","""Whoever learns an aspect of knowledge in order to teach it to people for the sake of attaining Allah's pleasure, Allah Almighty will grant him the reward of seventy prophets."
"294","""Indeed, even in Paradise, the people of Paradise will be in need of the scholars."
"295","""One moment spent seeking knowledge is better than a night of standing (in prayer), and one day spent seeking knowledge is better than three days of fasting."
"296","“When a student sits before his teacher, Allah Almighty opens seventy doors of mercy for him.”"
"297","""Whoever visited the scholars has visited me, and whoever shook hands with the scholars has shaken hands with me."
"298","""Whoever acts upon what he knows, Allah Almighty will grant him the inheritance of such knowledge which he does not possess."
"299","""The status of a Shaykh (spiritual teacher) among his people is the same as that of a Prophet among his community."
"300","“Prayer behind a religious scholar is equal to four thousand four hundred prayers.”"
"301","""The ink of the scholars is superior to the blood of the martyrs."
"302","""Most of the hypocrites of this Ummah are its reciters."
"303","""The worst scholars are those who go to the rulers and governors, and the best rulers and governors are those who go to the scholars."
"304","""A time will come upon my Ummah when the jurists will envy one another."
"306","""Looking at the face of a religious scholar is an act of worship."
"307","""I am the city of knowledge and Ali is its gate."
"308","""The death of a religious scholar is a loss that cannot be compensated and a gap that cannot be filled."
